---
description: Never put Node require/import in renderer or browser app scripts
globs: "{src/**/*.js,apps/**/*.js}"
alwaysApply: true
---
# Renderer / browser JS  no Node requires (CRITICAL)
Files under `src/*.js` and most `apps/**/*.js` run in Electron **webview/renderer**, not Node.
**NEVER** add at the top of these files:
- `require("...")` — including `lucide-static`, `@composio/core`, `electron`, `electron/main`, `fs`, `path`
- `import ... from "..."`
A single top-level `require` throws `require is not defined`. That script never runs. Symptoms: empty Runtime, dead buttons, broken shell language, broken OS Bridge, half-working desktop.
If you see a stray `require`/`import` at the top of `src/shell-commands.js`, `apps/scripts/app.js`, or any browser script, **delete that line immediately**.
`npm start` runs `scripts/check-browser-apps.js`, which auto-strips known bad injects and fails on remaining top-level requires.